@id n3_mab
# DRAFT
# Mab at the gate (night 3), from dusk until the knocks. She sees who comes and goes, nobody asks her, and she never eats the abbey's bread.
# Night 3 keeps its own; the other nights are game/chapters/common/lane/mab.talk. Alms once (n3_mab_alms): a heel of Fenchurch Street bread.
== start
(Mab sits against the wall by the gate, her clapper in her lap, her face wrapped to the eyes.)
Mab {warm}: Porter. You look worse every night. I say it kindly.
-> topics

== again
(She knocks her clapper once against the stones.)
Mab {wary}: Still here? So am I.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n3_mab_saw] What have you seen, Mab? -> saw
* [if bread_warned] [if not n3_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread, Mab? -> bread
* [if not n3_mab_alms] (Give her alms.) -> alms

== saw [set n3_mab_saw]
Mab {wary}: Everyone who goes in at that gate, and everyone who comes out. Nobody asks me.
Mab {afraid}: Last night something walked the lane after the bell. Taller than a man. It came from the corner of your wall.
Mab {afraid}: And the rooks came off your tower before Matins, all at once, screaming. Before your bell, porter. Not after.
-> topics

== bread [set n3_mab_bread]
Mab {cold}: Theirs? Never. Not a crumb in eleven years, and I've been hungry enough to eat straw.
Mab {wary}: Somebody's told you something about it. I can see it on you.
Mab {grave}: Good. Then I don't have to.
-> topics

== alms [set n3_mab_alms] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5]
(You drop a coin in the bowl at her feet.)
Mab {warm}: God keep you, porter. Here. It's not theirs. A baker on Fenchurch Street makes it.
(She sets a heel of bread on the step between you, wrapped in a cloth, and draws back.)
-> topics
